# FORGE Agent Guide

PostgreSQL-only. **Package: `forgex`** (import as `forge`). [Docs](https://tryforge.dev/docs) | `forge --help`

## Verify Changes

```bash
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test && bun lint && bun format
```

## Function Types

| Type | Use Case | Key Features |
|------|----------|--------------|
| Query | Read data | Cacheable, subscribable, `ctx.db()` |
| Mutation | Write data | `ctx.db()`, `ctx.http()`, `ctx.dispatch_job()`, opt-in transactional |
| Job | Background work | Retryable, progress tracking, `ctx.http()`, `ctx.progress()` |
| Cron | Scheduled | Leader-only, catch-up, `ctx.http()`, `ctx.log` |
| Workflow | Multi-step | Durable, compensatable, `ctx.step()`, `ctx.sleep()`, `ctx.http()` |

## Function Signatures & Attributes

```rust
// Query: cache, public, require_auth, require_role("x"), timeout=30, rate_limit(...), tables=["t1","t2"] (explicit deps for subscribe())
#[forge::query(cache = "5m", public)]
pub async fn get_users(ctx: &QueryContext) -> Result<Vec<User>> { }

// Mutation: require_auth, require_role("x"), timeout=30, rate_limit(...), transactional (opt-in TX wrapping)
#[forge::mutation(require_role("admin"))]
pub async fn create_user(ctx: &MutationContext, input: CreateUserInput) -> Result<User> { }

#[forge::mutation(transactional)]  // Wraps in BEGIN/COMMIT, jobs use outbox pattern
pub async fn transfer_funds(ctx: &MutationContext, input: TransferInput) -> Result<()> { }

// Job: timeout, priority, max_attempts, worker_capability, idempotent, retry
#[forge::job]
#[timeout = "30m"]
#[priority = "high"]  // background, low, normal, high, critical
#[retry(max_attempts = 5, backoff = "exponential", max_backoff = "5m")]
#[idempotent(key = "input.email")]
pub async fn process_order(ctx: &JobContext, input: OrderInput) -> Result<()> { }

// Cron: timezone, timeout, catch_up, catch_up_limit
#[forge::cron("0 9 * * *")]  // minute hour day month weekday
#[timezone = "America/New_York"]
#[catch_up]
pub async fn daily_report(ctx: &CronContext) -> Result<()> { }

// Workflow: version, timeout
#[forge::workflow]
#[version = 1]
#[timeout = "7d"]
pub async fn onboarding(ctx: &WorkflowContext, user: User) -> Result<()> { }
```

## Context Methods

```rust
// All contexts
ctx.db()                              // &PgPool
ctx.require_user_id()?                // Uuid or Unauthorized error
ctx.require_subject()?                // &str (for Firebase/Auth0/Clerk - non-UUID providers)
ctx.auth.has_role("admin")            // bool
ctx.env("KEY")                        // Option<String>
ctx.env_require("KEY")?               // Result<String>

// Mutation only
ctx.http()                            // &reqwest::Client
ctx.dispatch_job("job_name", args)?   // -> Uuid
ctx.start_workflow("wf_name", input)? // -> Uuid

// Job, Cron, Workflow only
ctx.http()                            // &reqwest::Client

// Job only
ctx.progress(50, "Processing...")?    // percentage, message
ctx.is_retry()                        // attempt > 1
ctx.is_last_attempt()                 // attempt >= max_attempts

// Cron only
ctx.is_late()                         // delay > 1 minute
ctx.log.info("msg", json!({}))        // structured logging

// Workflow only
ctx.step("name", || async { ... }).compensate(|r| async { ... }).run().await?
ctx.parallel().step("a", || ...).step("b", || ...).run().await?
ctx.sleep(Duration::from_days(30)).await?    // durable sleep
ctx.wait_for_event::<T>("event", timeout).await?
```

## Testing (In-File with Embedded DB)

```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use forge::testing::{TestDatabase, IsolatedTestDb};

    async fn setup_db(name: &str) -> (IsolatedTestDb, sqlx::PgPool) {
        let base = TestDatabase::embedded().await.unwrap();
        let db = base.isolated(name).await.unwrap();
        db.run_sql(&forge::get_internal_sql()).await.unwrap();
        db.migrate(Path::new("migrations")).await.unwrap();
        (db, db.pool().clone())
    }

    #[tokio::test]
    async fn test_example() {
        let (_db, pool) = setup_db("test_example").await;
        // Use sqlx::query() runtime queries, not macros
    }
}
```

Run: `cargo test`

## Test Contexts (Unit Tests)

```rust
use forge::testing::*;

// Query context
let ctx = TestQueryContext::builder()
    .as_user(Uuid::new_v4())
    .with_role("admin")
    .with_pool(pool)
    .build();

// Mutation context (with HTTP mocking and dispatch verification)
let ctx = TestMutationContext::builder()
    .as_user(id)
    .mock_http_json("https://api.example.com/*", json!({"ok": true}))
    .build();
ctx.dispatch_job("send_email", args).await?;
ctx.job_dispatch().assert_dispatched("send_email");
ctx.http().assert_called("https://api.example.com/*");

// Job context
let ctx = TestJobContext::builder("job_name")
    .as_retry(2)
    .with_max_attempts(5)
    .build();
```

## CLI Commands

```bash
forge new <name> --demo|--minimal    # Create project
forge dev                            # Start dev (embedded PG + backend + frontend)
forge dev --docker                   # Start with Docker Compose
forge add query|mutation|job|cron|workflow <name>
forge generate                       # Generate TypeScript types
forge migrate up|down|status         # Database migrations
forge check                          # Validate project
```

## Anti-Patterns

| Don't | Do |
|-------|-----|
| `tokio::sleep` in Workflow | `ctx.sleep()` |
| Destructure `$props()` | Keep reference |
| Poll with `query()` loop | `subscribe()` |
| `refetch()` after mutations | `SELECT forge_enable_reactivity('table')` in migrations |
| `ctx.auth.user_id().unwrap()` | `ctx.require_user_id()?` |
| Edit `frontend/src/lib/forge/` | Run `forge generate` |
| Dynamic SQL in subscribed query | Add `tables = [...]` for invalidation |
| Non-atomic data+job | Use `#[forge::mutation(transactional)]` |
| `{#if $store}` with nullable store | Copy to `$state` via `.subscribe()` |

