## Frontend (Svelte 5)

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { createSubscriptionStore, getForgeClient, createUser, type User } from '$lib/forge';

  let state = $state<{ loading: boolean; data: User[] | null }>({ loading: true, data: null });

  $effect(() => {
    if (!user) return;  // Gate on auth
    const store = createSubscriptionStore<object, User[]>('list_users', {});
    const unsub = store.subscribe(s => { state = { loading: s.loading, data: s.data }; });
    return () => { unsub(); store.unsubscribe(); };
  });

  // IMPORTANT: Call after login/logout to refresh SSE auth
  getForgeClient().reconnect();
</script>
```

**NEVER edit `frontend/src/lib/forge/`** — auto-generated by `forge generate`.

## Migrations

```sql
-- migrations/0001_initial.sql
-- @up
CREATE TABLE users (id UUID PRIMARY KEY, email VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL);
SELECT forge_enable_reactivity('users');

-- @down
SELECT forge_disable_reactivity('users');
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users;
```

## Structure

```
src/functions/  # One file per function (+ inline tests)
src/schema/     # #[forge::model], #[forge::forge_enum]
migrations/     # NNNN_name.sql (-- @up / -- @down)
frontend/       # Svelte 5 app
```

## Error Handling

```rust
use forge::prelude::*;  // Includes ForgeError, Result

// Common error variants
ForgeError::NotFound("User not found")      // 404
ForgeError::Unauthorized("Login required")  // 401
ForgeError::Forbidden("Admin only")         // 403
ForgeError::Validation("Invalid email")     // 400
ForgeError::Database(msg)                   // 500
```

## External Auth (JWT)

Forge validates JWTs from any provider (Firebase, Auth0, Clerk, Supabase, custom). Configure in `forge.toml`:

```toml
[auth]
jwt_algorithm = "RS256"              # HS256/HS384/HS512 or RS256/RS384/RS512
jwt_secret = "${JWT_SECRET}"         # For HMAC (HS*) algorithms
jwks_url = "https://..."             # For RSA (RS*) algorithms - provider's JWKS endpoint
jwt_issuer = "https://..."           # Expected `iss` claim
jwt_audience = "your-project-id"     # Expected `aud` claim
```

Frontend: Pass token getter to provider.

```typescript
// frontend/src/lib/auth.ts
export const getToken = () => yourAuthProvider.getIdToken() ?? Promise.resolve(null);
```

```svelte
<ForgeProvider url={PUBLIC_API_URL} getToken={getToken}><slot /></ForgeProvider>
```

Backend: External providers use string subjects, not UUIDs.

```rust
ctx.require_subject()?  // -> &str (for external providers)
ctx.require_user_id()?  // -> Uuid (for internal/UUID-based auth)
```

## Workflow

Schema → Migration → `forge add <type> <name>` → Register in main.rs → `forge generate`

## Code Quality

Idiomatic Rust | Small functions | Fail fast | No premature abstraction | `bun` only (not npm/yarn)
